const html =
  '<p>Koakademy includes six pre-packaged domain modules residing in <code>Modules/</code>. Each module provides dedicated Eloquent models, database migrations, Filament management resources, and portal endpoints. Modules can be enabled or disabled per institution without code changes.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. Announcements Module (<code>Modules\\Announcement</code>)</h2>\n<p>The Announcements module coordinates school-wide and targeted communications across all user portals:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Audience Targeting:</strong> Publish bulletins globally, or restrict visibility to specific schools, roles (e.g. Faculty only, Students only), academic departments, or degree programs.</li>\n<li><strong>Top Banner Alerts:</strong> Urgent alerts (such as typhoon class cancellations or emergency advisories) can be pinned as a high-visibility global banner across all portals.</li>\n<li><strong>Scheduled Publishing:</strong> Specify publication and expiration dates so announcements publish and archive automatically.</li>\n<li><strong>Rich Media &amp; Attachments:</strong> Supports rich text formatting, downloadable PDF memos, and embedded imagery.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. Cashier Module (<code>Modules\\Cashier</code>)</h2>\n<p>The Cashier module provides counter operations for tuition collections, miscellaneous fee payments, and daily financial reconciliation:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Rapid Counter Register:</strong> Barcode and ID scanner lookup pulls up student balances in under one second.</li>\n<li><strong>Official Receipt (OR) Registry:</strong> Sequenced, auditable receipt numbers with automatic voiding workflows and supervisor approval gates.</li>\n<li><strong>Multi-Tender Payments:</strong> Accept Cash, Cheques (with bank branch and clearing dates), POS credit/debit card terminals, and mobile e-wallets.</li>\n<li><strong>Cash Drawer Balancing:</strong> End-of-day reconciliation comparing physical cash drawer balances against expected electronic ledger totals.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>3. Inventory &amp; Asset Management (<code>Modules\\Inventory</code>)</h2>\n<p>The Inventory module tracks physical equipment, campus facilities, classroom furnishings, and IT hardware across buildings and rooms:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Asset Catalog &amp; Categorization:</strong> Classifies assets (Computer equipment, Laboratory instruments, Office furniture, AV equipment) with serial numbers and barcodes.</li>\n<li><strong>Location &amp; Room Tracking:</strong> Maps assets to specific buildings, floors, and classrooms (<code>Room</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Custodian Accountability:</strong> Issues Memorandum Receipts (MR) to faculty and staff members accountable for assigned hardware.</li>\n<li><strong>Maintenance &amp; Stock Ledger:</strong> Logs maintenance history, repair tickets, depreciation schedules, and inventory disposal.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>4. Library Management System (<code>Modules\\LibrarySystem</code>)</h2>\n<p>The Library System handles physical book cataloging, circulation desk operations, and student research archives:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Book Catalog &amp; Classification:</strong> Catalogs volumes with ISBN, Dewey Decimal classification, author profiles, and barcode tracking.</li>\n<li><strong>Circulation Desk:</strong> Fast barcode scanning for checkout and return transactions, enforcing borrowing periods based on user role (e.g. 3 days for students, 14 days for faculty).</li>\n<li><strong>Overdue Fines Engine:</strong> Automated daily fine calculations for late returns, with automatic clearance hold integration.</li>\n<li><strong>Theses &amp; Research Paper Archive:</strong> Digital repository for undergraduate theses, capstone projects, and faculty research papers with searchable abstracts.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>5. Notification Center (<code>Modules\\NotificationCenter</code>)</h2>\n<p>The Notification Center coordinates automated transactional communications across multiple channels:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Template Engine:</strong> Customizable notification templates with dynamic merge tags (e.g. <code>{student_name}</code>, <code>{amount_due}</code>, <code>{class_name}</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Multi-Channel Dispatch:</strong> Dispatches messages via database notifications (in-portal bell alerts), email (SMTP/SES), and SMS gateways.</li>\n<li><strong>Batch Broadcast Queues:</strong> Leverages background queue workers to broadcast notices to thousands of students without blocking web requests.</li>\n<li><strong>Event Triggers:</strong> Automated dispatches on enrollment approval, grade publication, payment receipt, and clearance holds.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>6. Student Medical Records (<code>Modules\\StudentMedicalRecords</code>)</h2>\n<p>The Clinic module provides confidential campus healthcare records with HIPAA-grade privacy isolation:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Student Health Profiles:</strong> Tracks blood type, chronic illnesses, severe allergies, immunization records, and emergency contact details.</li>\n<li><strong>Clinic Visit Encounters:</strong> Records date/time, presenting symptoms, nursing diagnosis, administered medication, and recommended action.</li>\n<li><strong>Medical Clearances:</strong> Issues digital medical clearances required for physical education, collegiate athletics, and internship deployment.</li>\n<li><strong>Confidentiality Boundaries:</strong> Clinic notes are strictly isolated: faculty and general administrative staff cannot access private health records.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>Module Marketplace &amp; Standalone Packages</h2>\n<p>Beyond the six bundled modules, Koakademy supports standalone Composer modules (such as the <a href="https://github.com/yukazakiri/koakademy-module-forms">Forms Module</a>) distributed via the <a href="https://github.com/yukazakiri/koakademy-modules">Koakademy Module Registry</a>.</p>\n<p>Administrators can toggle any installed module on or off from <strong>Administrators → Marketplace</strong> without redeploying the application image.</p>\n'
